Third-party files in this directory
===================================

Every file under vendor/ercot/ is byte-identical to its source.
vendor/MANIFEST.json records each file's source URL (or ercot/api-specs commit),
retrieval date, size and sha256; `python scripts/fetch_vendor.py verify` checks
them. Two files outside vendor/ercot/ are text taken from web pages, not copies
of a published file:

  ERCOT-TERMS-OF-USE.txt   the text of https://www.ercot.com/help/terms,
                           extracted from the page's HTML by
                           scripts/fetch_vendor.py: markup removed, wording
                           unchanged. Its hash is in MANIFEST.json.
  licenses/W3C-SOFTWARE-NOTICE-19980720.txt
                           the text of
                           https://www.w3.org/Consortium/Legal/copyright-software-19980720


ERCOT
-----

Files:
  ercot/api-specs/ews/        the ews/ folder of https://github.com/ercot/api-specs
                              at the commit pinned in MANIFEST.json
  ercot/developer.ercot.com/  the developer portal's search index and twelve
                              diagrams from https://developer.ercot.com/
  ERCOT-TERMS-OF-USE.txt      ERCOT's Website User Agreement

The ercot/api-specs repository carries no licence file. These files are
redistributed under section 5 of ERCOT's Website User Agreement
(https://www.ercot.com/help/terms, "Last updated: 07/20/2023"), which reads in
part:

  "The publicly available contents of this website may be used, reproduced,
  and redistributed, provided that the contents are not modified and that you
  maintain all copyright and other notices contained in the contents,
  including this Agreement."

Section 1 defines "this website" as ERCOT.com, "including any other sites that
may be accessed through ERCOT.com". Both sources are reached that way:
https://www.ercot.com/services/mdt links to https://developer.ercot.com, and the
portal's EWS specification page (https://developer.ercot.com/api_specifications/ews/ews/)
says "ERCOT Web Services' specifications are hosted on GitHub. Please navigate
to our API Specification Repository to find the latest content."

The files are therefore kept unmodified, their notices are kept, and the
Agreement is reproduced in ERCOT-TERMS-OF-USE.txt.

Section 9 of the Agreement reads:

  "The ERCOT logo, "ERCOT," and "The Texas Connection" are either trademarks
  or registered trademarks of ERCOT and may not be used without the prior
  written permission of ERCOT."

This project uses the name ERCOT only to say which market's interfaces it works
with, and uses no ERCOT logo; see ../NOTICE.

ERCOT provides this content "AS IS" without warranties of any kind (section 2
of the Agreement).


